README.rpm-dist
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PostgreSQL 18 engine patched for Babelfish, RPM set.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is the PostgreSQL engine modified for Babelfish for PostgreSQL (SQL Server
compatibility), built from
https://github.com/babelfish-for-postgresql/postgresql_modified_for_babelfish

It is installed next to, and independent of, the stock PGDG PostgreSQL 18
packages:

  Installation directory : /usr/babelfish-18
  Service                : babelfish_postgresql-18
  Data directory         : /var/lib/babelfish/18/data
  Setup script           : babelfish_postgresql-18-setup

Binaries are NOT added to /usr/bin (no update-alternatives) and the libraries
are NOT added to the system linker path; use the full path
(/usr/babelfish-18/bin/psql) or add the bin directory to PATH.

QUICKSTART
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Install the babelfish_postgresql18-server package (and
   babelfish_extensions_18 for the Babelfish extensions).

2. Initialize the cluster:

     /usr/babelfish-18/bin/babelfish_postgresql-18-setup initdb

3. Start it:

     systemctl enable --now babelfish_postgresql-18

Both this server and the stock PostgreSQL 18 service default to port 5432.
Change "port" in postgresql.conf if you run them on the same host.

Enabling Babelfish itself (shared_preload_libraries, CREATE EXTENSION
babelfishpg_tds, migration mode, ...) is described in the Babelfish
documentation at https://babelfishpg.org/ and needs the babelfish_extensions
package.

NOTES
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* The upgrade/check_upgrade modes of the setup script expect the previous
  major version of this same Babelfish engine (/usr/babelfish-17,
  /var/lib/babelfish/17/data). Babelfish clusters cannot be upgraded
  from a stock PostgreSQL cluster.
* No SELinux policy is shipped for this engine: the stock policy only labels
  /usr/pgsql-<version>/ paths.
